354502, -0.008664492517709732, 0.004854436963796616, 0.005492669530212879, 0.031357213854789734, -0.003835843177512288, -0.01986902393400669, -0.028572196140885353, -0.010295532643795013, -0.014647118747234344, -0.00011030063615180552, -0.013319078832864761, -0.00827768538147211, 0.028004879131913185, -0.015755968168377876, 0.0008219663868658245, 0.0004859271866735071, -0.00034309038892388344, -0.0319245308637619, -0.019443534314632416, 0.005698967259377241, 0.012177996337413788], "index": 9, "object": "embedding"}], "model": "text-embedding-3-small", "object": "list", "usage": {"prompt_tokens": 7402, "total_tokens": 7402}}, "input": {"input": ["--- Record 1971 ---\nComponent: SAP Build Process Automation\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Track Instances Using the Visibility Scenario Instances Application\nDescription: You can now track and monitor instances using the Visibility Scenario Instances application with the Standard User entitlement.See Track Instances Using Visibility Scenario Instances Application.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-11-12\nValid as Of: 2024-11-12\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1972 ---\nComponent: SAP Print service\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry,Other\nTitle: Monitoring Connection Status\nDescription: Monitor the connection status of SAP Print service to third-party output management systems.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-11-12\nValid as Of: 2024-11-12\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1973 ---\nComponent: Continuous Integration & Delivery\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: New Region\nDescription: SAP Continuous Integration and Delivery can now also be consumed in the Switzerland (Zurich) and US East (VA) regions. See Regional Availability.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-11-11\nValid as Of: 2024-11-11\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1974 ---\nComponent: Cloud Identity Services\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry,Kyma,Neo\nTitle: Identity Directory API\nDescription: We have introduced a new implementation of the PATCH method of the Identity Directory API for all tenants in all Cloud Identity Services data centers except the ones in North America and Europe. The behavior of the new implementation is the same as the old one.  The implementation in the remaining data centers is planned for November 25, 2024.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: Restricted Availability\nType: Announcement\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-11-11\nValid as Of: 2024-11-11\nVersion: 26936\n\n--- Record 1975 ---\nComponent: Document Management Service\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Change of Default Credential Type for Service Key\nDescription: The default credential type for Document Management Service, Integration Option service key has been updated. It's now 'binding-secret' instead of 'instance-secret'.  We made this change because xsuaa has deprecated the credential type 'instance-secret'.  This change only affects service instances that are updated with new service key.  Action: Check whether you are affected by the change. If you are impacted, ensure that your application is adjusted to work with 'binding-secret 'credential type before this change is activated.  See Creating and Updating a Service Instance and Service Key.\nAction: Required\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-11-08\nValid as Of: 2024-11-08\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1976 ---\nComponent: Document Management Service\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Superdomain URL for SAP Document Management Service\nDescription: SAP is migrating its products to a common cloud.sap superdomain to address browser isolation and privacy issues caused by current domain-specific URLs.  This change aims to improve integration scenarios using iFrames or cross-origin requests, which are affected by modern browser security features.  These changes apply only to new subscriptions and do not impact existing customers.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-11-08\nValid as Of: 2024-11-08\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1977 ---\nComponent: Kyma Runtime\nEnvironment: Kyma\nTitle: SAP BTP Operator module: Documentation\nDescription: We are happy to announce the publication of the SAP BTP Operator's documentation.  For general information on the module, see SAP BTP Operator Module. For detailed descriptions of the module's features, operations, and usage guidance, see the comprehensive set of related documents, including Preconfigured Credentials and Access, Creating Service Instances and Service Bindings, Deleting Service Bindings and Service Instances, and more.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-11-07\nValid as Of: 2024-11-07\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1978 ---\nComponent: Kyma Runtime\nEnvironment: Kyma\nTitle: Telemetry module: Update to version 1.26.0\nDescription: The new version brings the following improvements:      Metrics: You can now collect metrics about the Kubernetes persistent volumes that are bound to your workloads: Just enable the new selector for volume metrics in the runtime input of your MetricPipeline resources. (#1301). For details, see Activate Runtime Metrics.      Traces: The deployment name of the trace gateway is now consistently named telemetry-trace-gateway. This change does not affect users (#652).      Logs: Update to Fluent Bit 3.1.9 (#1503).      Improved resource request settings for several components of the Telemetry module (#1532).    \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-10-23\nValid as Of: 2024-11-06\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1979 ---\nComponent: SAP Build Apps\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Mobile\nDescription: The Android builds now support only devices with 64-bit processors. We're discontinuing support for Android devices with 32-bit processors to decrease the", "Action: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-10-23\nValid as Of: 2024-11-06\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1979 ---\nComponent: SAP Build Apps\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Mobile\nDescription: The Android builds now support only devices with 64-bit processors. We're discontinuing support for Android devices with 32-bit processors to decrease the file sizes of these builds. The application preview for 32-bit devices remains supported.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-11-06\nValid as Of: 2024-11-06\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1980 ---\nComponent: SAP Build Process Automation\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Create and Manage Process Variants\nDescription: You use process variants to create a process with preconfigured settings. The variant is made available to business users and reduces the amount of technical detail and options to guide users by offering a subset of process design options.For more information, see Create and Manage Process Variants.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-11-06\nValid as Of: 2024-11-06\nVersion: Cloud\n\n", "--- Record 4041 ---\nComponent: SAP Start\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Availability of foundation service plan\nDescription: The foundation service plan for SAP Build Work Zone, standard edition is now available. The foundation service plan extends the availability of SAP Start to all customers who have subscribed at least one of the integrated SAP Cloud business solutions.  This enables using SAP Start for free up to a predefined limit of Active Users, as specified in the SAP BTP Service Description Guide.  For more information, see Commercialization Aspects.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2023-10-19\nValid as Of: 2023-10-19\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 4042 ---\nComponent: SAP Start\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Availability of setup booster that subscribes to the foundation service plan\nDescription: Customers who do not have a subscription to SAP Build Work Zone, standard edition, can now use a booster to set up SAP Start and subscribe to the foundation service plan, instead of the standard service plan.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2023-10-19\nValid as Of: 2023-10-19\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 4043 ---\nComponent: Mobile Services\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Supported versions for Cloud Build Service\nDescription: We've updated the supported versions for the Cloud Build service:    October 2023 - Mobile Development Kit SDK version, Android and iOS versions, and notes      September 2023 - Mobile Development Kit SDK version, Android and iOS versions, and notes      August 2023      Mobile Development Kit SDK version, iOS version, and notes      SAP Asset Manager SDK version, Android and iOS versions, and notes          See Supported Build Types, Client Types, Packaging Details, and Build Options  \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-01-01\nValid as Of: 2023-10-18\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 4044 ---\nComponent: Mobile Services\nEnvironment: Neo\nTitle: Supported versions for Cloud Build Service\nDescription: We've updated the supported versions for the Cloud Build service:    October 2023 (2305 PL06)    Fiori Packaged UI5 version and iOS version      Custom Fiori Client iOS version      Mobile Development Kit SDK version, iOS versions and notes          September 2023 (2305 PL05)    Fiori Packaged SDK version and iOS version      Custom Fiori Client SDK version and iOS version      Mobile Development Kit SDK version and notes          August 2023 (2305 PL04): Mobile Development Kit SDK version, iOS version, and notes      See Supported Build Types, Client Types, Packaging Details, and Build Options  \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-01-01\nValid as Of: 2023-10-18\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 4045 ---\nComponent: SAP Build Process Automation\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Change Agent Groups to the Any Type\nDescription: You can change agent groups from type Login or Machine to type Any to make their content easier to manage.  See Change Agent Groups to the Any Type.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2023-10-17\nValid as Of: 2023-10-17\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 4046 ---\nComponent: SAP Build Process Automation\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Change Language and Theme in Desktop Agent 3\nDescription: You can now change the language and theme in desktop agent 3 under System /Settings. You can also rearrange the columns in the trace viewer by right-clicking on the respective column.  See Accessibility Features for Desktop Agent 3.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2023-10-17\nValid as Of: 2023-10-17\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 4047 ---\nComponent: SAP Build Process Automation\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Without Excel Application Activities\nDescription: Without Excel application activities are a subset of activities inside MS Excel SDK. You can now use these activities even if you don't have the MS Excel application. See Without Excel Application Activities.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2023-10-17\nValid as Of: 2023-10-17\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 4048 ---\nComponent: SAP Intelligent Robotic Process Automation\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Configuring Web Browsers\nDescription: Our mutation observer is now improved to detect webpage unloads in the Chrome or Edge browser. See Configuring Web Browsers.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2023-10-17\nValid as Of: 2023-10-17\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 4049 ---\nComponent: SAP Intelligent Robotic Process Automation\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Without Excel Application Activities\nDescription: Without Excel application activities are a subset of activities inside MS Excel SDK. You can now use these activities even if you don't have the MS Excel application. See Without Excel Application Activities.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2023-10-", "Version: Cloud\n\n--- Record 4049 ---\nComponent: SAP Intelligent Robotic Process Automation\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Without Excel Application Activities\nDescription: Without Excel application activities are a subset of activities inside MS Excel SDK. You can now use these activities even if you don't have the MS Excel application. See Without Excel Application Activities.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2023-10-17\nValid as Of: 2023-10-17\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 4050 ---\nComponent: SAP Build Process Automation\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: New SAP Fiori UI5 Theme: Horizon\nDescription: With this release, only the following themes are supported in SAP Build Process Automation for Lobby, Store, Monitor, and Settings:    Morning Horizon    Evening Horizon  Horizon High Contrast White  Horizon High Contrast Black   \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2023-10-16\nValid as Of: 2023-10-16\nVersion: Cloud\n\n", "--- Record 1601 ---\nComponent: SAP Omnichannel Promotion Pricing\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Loyalty Points Multiplier\nDescription: You can now maintain a  Loyalty Points Multiplier as reward in the Maintain Promotions app to define by which value previously calculated and applied loyalty points should be multiplied. For this, a new type of price derivation rule BenefitMultiplierPriceDerivationRule is available as of Client API version 16.0.  For more information, see Granting Loyalty Points and Price Calculation with Loyalty Points Multiplier (XML).\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2022-01-01\nValid as Of: 2025-01-22\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1602 ---\nComponent: Variant Configuration\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Pre-Production - Configurations API – Raise Conflict for Non-Unique Inferences from Multiple Rows of a Variant Table\nDescription: When a characteristic value could not be set because a selection on a variant table resulted in more than one row, an exception used to be raised and the configuration service endpoint prompted an error. This behavior has been changed by not raising an exception anymore but signaling a conflict in the configuration results in the same way as LO-VC does it.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-12-12\nValid as Of: 2025-01-22\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1603 ---\nComponent: Variant Configuration\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Pre-Production – Configurations API -– AVC Forwarding – Ensure Sort Order Remains Stable Between Requests\nDescription: The order of existing possible values could have changed after a PATCH request, that is, setting a value during the configuration while using AVC forwarding. This issue has been corrected.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-12-12\nValid as Of: 2025-01-22\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1604 ---\nComponent: Variant Configuration\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Pre-Production – Configurations API – AVC Forwarding – Possible Values: Include pre-defined characteristic values\nDescription: Valid pre-defined characteristic values used to be omitted from the returned list of possible values of date and numeric characteristics if a restricted dynamic domain was returned by AVC. This issue has been corrected.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-12-12\nValid as Of: 2025-01-22\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1605 ---\nComponent: Variant Configuration\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Pre-Production – Configurations API –Exclude Globally Assigned Characteristics from Configuration Results\nDescription: In certain scenarios, characteristics are assigned to classes and products only for internal purposes, for example, if they are used in object dependencies but not assigned to a class of the product. These so-called globally assigned characteristics are now filtered out in the service responses and are not persisted anymore with the configuration results. They can still show up in the configuration engine trace.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-12-12\nValid as Of: 2025-01-22\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1606 ---\nComponent: Variant Configuration\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Pre-Production – Knowledgebases API – New Filter to Read Variant Table ContentPre-Production – Knowledgebases API – New Filter to Read Variant Table Content\nDescription: There is an enhancement of endpoint GET /api/v2/knowledgebases/{kbId}/variantTables/{variantTableId} that allows to read the content of a variant table: new IN operator for the parameter $filter allows more advanced table selects in the form of $filter=<characteristic name> IN (<list of characteristic values>).   See: API Definition and Development Guide for SAP Variant Configuration and Pricing.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-12-12\nValid as Of: 2025-01-22\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1607 ---\nComponent: SAP Build Process Automation\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Best Practices - Capturing Specific Elements\nDescription: To capture specific elements such as the Save File dialog or popups in the SAP WebGUI application, we recommend capturing them as a web page.See: Guidelines for the SAP GUI Technology Automation\nAction: Recommended\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-01-21\nValid as Of: 2025-01-21\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1608 ---\nComponent: Cloud Identity Services\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry,Kyma,Neo\nTitle: Off-Cycle Upgrade\nDescription: Cloud Identity Services have been upgraded.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-01-21\nValid as Of: 2025-01-21\nVersion: 27307\n\n--- Record 1609 ---\nComponent: Graph\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Improved visualization of actions and functions\nDescription: The visualization of actions and functions in the Graph Navigator have been enhanced. For more information, see Actions and Functions.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Intelligent Technologies\nLatest Revision: 2025-01-21\nValid as Of: ", "2025-01-21\nVersion: 27307\n\n--- Record 1609 ---\nComponent: Graph\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Improved visualization of actions and functions\nDescription: The visualization of actions and functions in the Graph Navigator have been enhanced. For more information, see Actions and Functions.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Intelligent Technologies\nLatest Revision: 2025-01-21\nValid as Of: 2025-01-21\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1610 ---\nComponent: Kyma Runtime\nEnvironment: Kyma\nTitle: Istio module: Update to version 1.13.0\nDescription: We have updated the internal structure that holds Istio Operator. This ensures that the module remains up-to-date with the latest upstream Istio dependencies.  This version of the Istio module includes Istio 1.24.1 and Envoy 1.32.2.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-01-21\nValid as Of: 2025-01-21\nVersion: Cloud\n\n", "--- Record 291 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: Software Components\nDescription: As of release 2508, for sub packages created in software component ZLOCAL, workbench requests are no longer required.  For more information, see Software Components.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-08-25\nValid as Of: 2025-08-15\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2508\n\n--- Record 292 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: Source Event Filter\nDescription: You can now restrict the sending of events by defining filters for event topics. These filters can now also be created directly for event payload properties.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-08-15\nValid as Of: 2025-08-15\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2508\n\n--- Record 293 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: SQL Service: INSERT and DELETE on Writable CDS View Entities\nDescription: In data integration scenarios, users can access data in an ABAP system from an external consumer, using the SQL service and the ODBC driver for ABAP. So far, users can query data in exposed CDS view entities, and this was a read-only scenario, where SELECT statements could be used.   Now, the SQL service can also be used to change data in exposed writable CDS view entities using INSERT and DELETE statements. Use cases for INSERT and DELETE in such a data integration scenario include: full replication of data from another system into the ABAP system or bringing data into staging tables that will be later used for your custom ABAP coding.  For more information, see Changing ABAP-Managed Data from External Applications.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-08-15\nValid as Of: 2025-08-15\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2508\n\n--- Record 294 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: Success Log for Processed Events\nDescription: It is now possible to configure a log for successfully processed events.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-08-15\nValid as Of: 2025-08-15\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2508\n\n--- Record 295 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: Technical Monitoring: SQL Statement Analysis app\nDescription: With this app, you can analyze the performance and resource consumption of SQL statements within a selectable time range.  See SQL Statement Analysis.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-06-05\nValid as Of: 2025-08-15\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2508\n\n--- Record 296 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: View Object Relationships\nDescription: With this feature, you can view inbound and outbound relationships for logged objects in business event logging. You can also navigate across object components.  For more information, see Display Business Events by Objects.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-08-15\nValid as Of: 2025-08-15\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2508\n\n--- Record 297 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: What's New for SAP Joule for Developers, ABAP AI Capabilities\nDescription: You can find the What's New for SAP Joule for developers, ABAP AI capabilities here: What's New for Joule for Developers, ABAP AI Capabilities.  Note  To leverage Joule's capabilities, you need to purchase an additional license: For SAP BTP ABAP environment, SAP S/4HANA Cloud Public Edition, and SAP S/4HANA Cloud Private Edition, see SAP Note 3571857  .\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-08-15\nValid as Of: 2025-08-15\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2508\n\n--- Record 298 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: XCO Library\nDescription: XCO XSLX: You can now customize the text alignment of cells. You can also customize your worksheet with tab coloring, merging and unmerging cells, and much more.  For more information, see XLSX Write Access.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-08-15\nValid as Of: 2025-08-15\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2508\n\n--- Record 299 ---\nComponent: Joule\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: New Use Cases Now Supported in Sales for SAP S/4HANA Cloud Private Edition\nDescription: The following transactional use cases are now supported in Sales for SAP S/4HANA Cloud Private Edition:    Fetch sales order details  Fetch sales order fulfillment issues  Fetch sales order document flow  Fetch details of outbound deliveries  Perform changes to sales order fields  Provide issue resolution for sales order fulfilment issues  Create sales documents with reference  Fetch billing document information  Navigate to the respective apps  \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business:", "Description: The following transactional use cases are now supported in Sales for SAP S/4HANA Cloud Private Edition:    Fetch sales order details  Fetch sales order fulfillment issues  Fetch sales order document flow  Fetch details of outbound deliveries  Perform changes to sales order fields  Provide issue resolution for sales order fulfilment issues  Create sales documents with reference  Fetch billing document information  Navigate to the respective apps  \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Sales\nLatest Revision: 2025-08-11\nValid as Of: 2025-08-15\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 300 ---\nComponent: Cloud Identity Services\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry,Kyma,Neo\nTitle: Off-Cycle Upgrade\nDescription: Cloud Identity Services have been upgraded.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-08-14\nValid as Of: 2025-08-14\nVersion: 28174\n\n", "--- Record 1901 ---\nComponent: SAP Advanced Financial Closing\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Change Planned Start Dialog Adjusted\nDescription: The dialog to change the planned start of a task in the Process Closing Tasks app has been adjusted so that it now has the same appearance as the corresponding dialog in the Manage Closing Task Lists app.  App affected:  Process Closing Tasks\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Finance\nLatest Revision: 2024-10-31\nValid as Of: 2024-11-17\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1902 ---\nComponent: SAP Advanced Financial Closing\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: SAP Build Process Automation Integration\nDescription: SAP Advanced Financial Closing now supports integration with SAP Build Process Automation. This new capability allows you to trigger workflows designed in SAP Build Process Automation directly from the SAP Advanced Financial Closing environment.  Caution  This integration can't be used in parallel to the stand-alone integration described under Process Automation Integration Based on ABAP.  More information:  User guide:  How to Create Tasks  How to Process Tasks  Integration of Tasks of Type Workflow    Administration guide:  SAP Build Process Automation Integration for SAP Advanced Financial Closing      Apps affected:  Manage Closing Task Lists  Process Closing Tasks  Specify Communication Systems  \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Finance\nLatest Revision: 2024-10-31\nValid as Of: 2024-11-17\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1903 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: Business Catalog for Key User Adaptation\nDescription: The business catalog SAP_CORE_BC_EXT_FLEX is deprecated. It is replaced by the business catalog SAP_CORE_BC_EXT_FLX_CUS_PC. This business catalog provides permissions that are needed for key user adaptation in SAPUI5 applications. Please update your roles accordingly.  For more information, see Adapting SAP Fiori UIs at Runtime - Key User Adaptation.\nAction: Required\nLifecycle: Deprecated\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-10-10\nValid as Of: 2024-11-15\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2411\n\n--- Record 1904 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: ABAP Development Tools for Eclipse: ATC Check \"Usage of Released APIs\" Can Be Run on Key User and ABAP Cloud Objects\nDescription: The ATC check \"Usage of Released APIs\" has been modified. It can now also run on a set of objects containing objects with ABAP Language Version \"Key User\" and \"ABAP for Cloud Development\". The check behaves as follows:       For objects with ABAP Language Version \"Standard\", the check checks the usage of the released APIs for the ABAP language version configured in the check.       For objects with ABAP Language Version \"ABAP for Cloud Development\", the check checks the usage of released APIs for cloud development.      For objects with ABAP Language Version \"Key User\", the check checks the usage of released APIs for key user.    \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-11-15\nValid as Of: 2024-11-15\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2411\n\n--- Record 1905 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: ABAP Development Tools for Eclipse: Clearing Coverage Results\nDescription: You can now clear your coverage results in the ABAP Coverage view.  See Evaluating ABAP Unit Code Coverage Results.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-11-15\nValid as Of: 2024-11-15\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2411\n\n--- Record 1906 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: ABAP Development Tools for Eclipse: Creating an ABAP Cloud Project in the Context of the  SAP BTP ABAP environment\nDescription: You no longer need a service key when creating an ABAP cloud project in the context of  SAP BTP ABAP environment. You now need to enter the ABAP service instance URL. The process is now the same as in the context of SAP S/4HANA Cloud ABAP environment.   See Creating an ABAP Cloud Project.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-11-15\nValid as Of: 2024-11-15\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2411\n\n--- Record 1907 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: ABAP Development Tools for Eclipse: Creating Launchpad App Descriptor Items\nDescription: You can now create launchpad app descriptor items that are required to call applications from the SAP Fiori launchpad.  See Working with Launchpad App Descriptor Items.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: nan\nLatest Revision: 2024-11-15\nValid as Of: 2024-11-15\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2411\n\n--- Record 1908 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: ABAP Development Tools for Eclipse: Displaying Field Characteristics for RAP Types in the Element Information Popup\nDescription: The Element Information popup (F2) for RAP types shows additional field characteristics information such as mandatory:create, mandatory:execute or readonly. The displayed field characteristics vary based on the RAP operation type.  See RAP - FieldCharacteristics.\nAction", " ABAP Environment 2411\n\n--- Record 1908 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: ABAP Development Tools for Eclipse: Displaying Field Characteristics for RAP Types in the Element Information Popup\nDescription: The Element Information popup (F2) for RAP types shows additional field characteristics information such as mandatory:create, mandatory:execute or readonly. The displayed field characteristics vary based on the RAP operation type.  See RAP - FieldCharacteristics.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-11-15\nValid as Of: 2024-11-15\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2411\n\n--- Record 1909 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: ABAP Development Tools for Eclipse: Displaying the Original WSDL in a SOAP Provider Model\nDescription: You can now display the original WSDL file that you used to create a SOAP provider model.  See Creating SOAP Service Providers.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: nan\nLatest Revision: 2024-11-15\nValid as Of: 2024-11-15\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2411\n\n--- Record 1910 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: ABAP Development Tools for Eclipse: Multi-Dimensional Analysis App Generator\nDescription: You can now use the multi-dimensional analysis app generator wizard to create all ABAP development objects that are needed to build, expose, and deploy a multi-dimensional analysis Fiori app.  See Generating Multi-Dimensional Analysis Applications.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-11-15\nValid as Of: 2024-11-15\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2411\n\n"], "parameters": {"model": "text-embedding-3-small"}}, "key": "embeddings_629f60fcb341ad220ab79ee4947e7cf09913bd558a74ebbf2cfd2a7ec5071b1b_v2"}